Lets skate-host report each jump's spin with the score: the half turns the
scoring counts (the same tolerance short of each 180 it scores spins with),
signed by the board's heading, plus the stance the jump left the ground in, a
jump counter and a trick counter, so the addon's HUD can name spins the way
Skate 3 does ("Kickflip 360", "FS Half-Cab"). Applied on top of
skate-host-hud.patch and skate-host-stance.patch (it adds fields to their
Score). Same license as the files it changes (Apache-2.0).

diff --git a/skate/crates/skate-host/src/physics/bridge.rs b/skate/crates/skate-host/src/physics/bridge.rs
index 98afc5f..1097a70 100644
--- a/skate/crates/skate-host/src/physics/bridge.rs
+++ b/skate/crates/skate-host/src/physics/bridge.rs
@@ -41,6 +41,21 @@ pub struct Score {
     pub fakie: bool,
     /// Riding with the opposite foot forward from the natural stance.
     pub switch: bool,
+    /// The latest jump's spin in half turns, rounded the way the scoring
+    /// does (its tolerance short of each 180), signed by the board's heading:
+    /// positive turns counter-clockwise seen from above. Held after landing
+    /// until the next jump.
+    pub spin: i32,
+    /// Counts jumps; goes up as each one leaves the ground.
+    pub jump: u32,
+    /// Whether the skater is in the air now.
+    pub air: bool,
+    /// The stance the latest jump left the ground in.
+    pub takeoff_fakie: bool,
+    pub takeoff_switch: bool,
+    /// Counts tricks the scoring has announced, so the same trick twice in a
+    /// row still reads as two.
+    pub tricks: u32,
 }
